       RowBox[{"\"\<ipr\>\"", ",", "zzIPRPlots"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
    "zzSettingsUsed"}], "]"}], ";"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"966d6692-\
b6c9-f947-8905-66591381c3a7"],

Cell["\<\
To inspect a full eigenket at one g without rerunning the sweep: \
zzOneED=zzEdgeED[1/10,zzUsed,zzSettingsUsed[\"EDTolerance\"]]; then use the \
unchanged sectorTable[zzOneED] and eigenket[zzOneED,sector,level]. Rerun 10.4 \
onward for a new parameter set; no kernel reset is needed. Every spectrum, \
entropy, and IPR plot uses Joined->False and all supplied g values. The \
g-axis ticks are readable axis labels, not a second sampling grid. MarkerSize \
defaults to 3 points in zzSettings; open partner markers are slightly larger. \
For a style-only update, reevaluate the shared definitions in 10.2 and the \
plot/export cells with the retained data. Changing zzGGrid requires \
recomputing 10.5. Matching spectra do not impose matching eigenstate \
observables.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bfe3cd9-7296-d849-a1e6-4e2e7e587da9"]
}, Closed]],

